WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.480
Whoa... We really have a convenience store.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.230
This isn't good, is it?

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.860
Of course it isn't good!

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.270
Definitely not good.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.490
I-In any case... let's go a bit closer.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:13.740
Are we going in?

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:14.410
No...

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.030
What?

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.990
Well, you know... I-It may be a fake one, so...

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.540
Fa-- What?! What do you mean by "fake one"?

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.380
Whoa...

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.130
This is a real convenience store!

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.800
"Opening Sale"

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.800
Hey... Coconuts...

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:34.090
Hm?

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.220
Why do you look like you're enjoying this?

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:36.930
What?!

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.970
Isn't having a convenience
store bad news for you?

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:40.930
She's right.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:45.480
O-Of course it is! This is a huge
problem for our dagashi shop!

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:49.610
But it's not just me!
To can't stop smirking, either!

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:49.610
"Smirk, smirk, smirk..."

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:52.690
O-Of course! It's a convenience
store we're talking about!

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.780
This is big news in the boonies like this!

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.960
Hey, you kids!

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.760
Why are you loitering in front of the store?

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.410
You're in the way of other customers!

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.550
Or is it possible you don't know
how an automatic door works?

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.310
I can't believe this. Come with me!

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.310
What's with him? He's scary.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.060
More importantly, who's that?

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.480
The door opens and closes
on its own, so be careful.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.610
Whoa!

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.900
"Welcome"

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.160
--Welcome!

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.530
--Welcome!
--Welcome!

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:07.410
Wh-Whoa... It's a convenience store!

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.620
It's warm in here.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.420
This place has tons of manga!

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.470
Wait... You said "Welcome" just now.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.130
Looks like you noticed.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.260
My name is Yutaka Beni.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.220
"Yutaka Beni"

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:24.010
Convenience stores are a brilliant,
perfected part of our culture!

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.810
I came all the way out here to spread that idea!

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.810
I'm the manager of this store,
Towns Mart, Kashigahama Branch!

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.060
A pleasure to meet you!

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:34.050
He's weird...

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:35.560
Manager?

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.330
Indeed.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.820
Nowadays, you can get anything
at a convenience store, and yet,

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.490
there seem to be many
anachronistic stores in this town.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:48.330
For example, that dagashi shop.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:53.290
Just as the weak in nature are
eliminated through natural selection.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:57.960
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.540
Just as a stagnant river turns rotten.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.960
A world that does not change
heads only towards death.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.840
Therefore, I will bring it back to life.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.550
I will change this town!

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:09.720
I-I don't get what he's saying at all,
but he creeps me out.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.600
Yeah, he may have a few screws loose.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.100
That's not the point! He's saying
he's gonna shut down the dagashi shop!　

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:15.560
What...?

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.320
W-W-W-Wait, I can't have that!

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.610
Hm? And why might that be?

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:24.990
Well... My family runs that dagashi shop,
so our life will be, you know...

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:25.860
I see.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.740
Then I suggest that you take
a good hard look at reality.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.830
This is the publications section with a
wide variety of manga and magazines.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:37.750
"Adult Magazines"

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:36.790
C-Coconuts! They have lots of dirty--

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.590
We carry daily necessities, stationery,
and food including condiments.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.470
Tea, alcohol, juice and soda.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.850
A whole variety of ready-to-eat foods and bento!

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:51.600
A photocopier, a fax machine, an ATM...
and friendly employees!

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:55.850
In short, you can find anything
and everything at our store!

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:57.730
It really is impressive...

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.570
Dirty magazines, too.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:01.780
That's not all.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:06.860
I strongly suggest you check out our
pride and joy, the snack section.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:13.370
These are made with the world's best
ingredients by a first-class pastry chef!

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.290
This is Towns Mart Kashigahama's
specially prepared section.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:22.130
The Special Sweets corner... by Yutaka Beni!

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.420
Wow! This is amazing!

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.260
"Whole Cakes - 3,500 yen each (plus tax)"

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.260
They're cute!

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.300
Right?

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:33.520
Do you realize now how terribly
old-fashioned dagashi shops are?

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:35.890
Coconuts...

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:38.280
What's the matter? Are you
too stunned to say anything?

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:39.860
Yutaka...

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:40.270
Hm?

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.150
These won't sell... They're too expensive.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:49.280
What? Too expensive, you say?

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.870
Well... I think that convenience store customers

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.290
\would probably prefer cheaper items instead.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:01.540
Things that are simple
and cheap... For example...

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:06.170
...things like this dagashi that
you can buy for 10 yen or so.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.170
"Orange Gum"

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.130
D-Dagashi?!

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.930
Yeah, I think that if you carry things like this,

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:14.930
not only children but also adult
customers would readily buy them.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:21.560
"BANG!"

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:21.560
I see...! He's right!

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.520
Do you know what you're doing?

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.150
What?

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.490
If they carry dagashi at their store...

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:28.780
Ah! Shoot...

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:32.990
It's true... She's absolutely right.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:36.580
And yet, he said that without
the slightest hint of fear.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.260
What a virtuous boy!

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:44.840
From now on, I'll face him
with respect as a rival!

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:47.840
Hm? Why are you crying?

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:50.340
I'm not crying.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.640
I'm definitely not crying!

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:55.920
And so, and so...

00:06:56.890 --> 00:06:59.600
A convenience store?! Did you check them out?

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.350
"...A convenience store?"

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.600
"Did you check them out?"

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.600
"Did you check them out?"
"them = dirty magazines"

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:01.600
More or less...

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.980
I see... Men are vulnerable
to those things, so...

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:03.110
"I see... Men are"

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:04.110
"vulnerable to those things, so..."

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:06.110
"vulnerable to those things, so..."
"those things = dirty magazines"

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.110
Hm? Yeah...

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.110
Listen. Don't get too carried away, okay?

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:08.110
"Listen. Don't get too carried away, okay?"

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:10.360
"Listen. Don't get too carried away, okay?"
"(dirty magazines-wise)"

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:10.360
What? What're you talking about?

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:16.870
They're attracting lots of people...
while we're struggling.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:16.870
"Opening Sale"

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:19.870
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.500
I'm home... Well, no one's--

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:27.280
You're late... dagashi shop boy!

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.880
Wh-What're you doing here?!

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:31.760
What...?

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.890
When a customer visits your shop,
you should start by greeting them, right?!

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.680
What?! I-I'm sorry.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.890
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:40.890
More importantly...

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:44.730
...to tell you the truth, there's an important
matter that I wish to discuss with you.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.400
Um, discuss what?

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.610
I'll get straight to the point.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:50.940
Kokonotsu!

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:52.400
Would you like to work at our store?!

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.450
Wait, what?

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:56.160
What?

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:00.910
Convenience stores are great.
I love convenience stores.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.870
O-Okay...

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:05.920
The strange relief you feel when you
stop by in the middle of the night...

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:11.050
The scare you feel from the noise of that
glowing thing that zaps bugs...

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:15.300
The ashtrays on the corners where construction
workers come seeking a place to smoke...

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.220
And, in a remote--

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.930
Wait, wait! Why are you only
talking about the less savory parts?

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:21.810
Because I love those parts, too!

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.940
Of course, that's just the tip of the iceberg!
What do you think?!

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:27.800
I'm not quite sure what to think.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:32.190
Listen, I have to keep this
dagashi shop open at any--

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.320
I'll pay you 850 yen an hour.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:36.660
E-Eight hundred...!

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:39.720
That's an exceptionally good wage.
I'm making a generous offer to you.

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.700
"The average hourly wage in this town is 750 yen."

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:44.160
Well, that isn't the issue. I'm just...

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.170
I see... So it's not the amount... Then...

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:56.180
...do you perhaps like pleasures
of the dirty variety?

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:02.060
Convenience stores carry books and
magazines that are somewhat dirty.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:04.980
Of course, buying them with
people around is very risky.

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:07.940
So? What're you getting at?

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.430
What if I were to say that if you join the crew,

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:13.190
you can buy them without being seen by anyone.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.700
I can... buy them?

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.700
Of course, that's one of the perks of the job.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:23.080
Go ahead, take them...

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:27.710
But know that once you do,
you've agreed to join our crew.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.710
Now, make your decision.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.550
What... should I do?

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:39.730
Hotaru...

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:49.060
I won't find the dirty pleasures
I seek in those magazines.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:53.070
More importantly, I'll grab
them with my own two hands!

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:58.490
Hm... I see...

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:01.410
Now that it's come to this,
I'll have to use my last resort.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:03.860
What? There's more?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.080
This is a job magazine that
has our store information.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:12.460
The entire crew made it together so that
everyone who sees it wants to come!

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:14.960
"A work environment where the smiles never stop!"

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.960
It makes you want to work with us, right?!

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:18.970
Whoa... They used the world's
most superficial phrase...

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:23.010
There was one girl who was shy
or something and wasn't feeling it,

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:25.020
but I'm sure with time she'll open up, right?

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:31.480
I can understand how she feels.
I don't think she's going to open up to you.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:33.480
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.530
Now, come and join our crew!

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:38.030
"Shikada Dagashi"
"Convenience Store, Job Magazine, and..."

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:36.350
Err...

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:38.030
Sorry, it won't work...

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:16.510
"Next time: Hajime Owari, Chocoball, and..."

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:11.330
Next time. "Hajime Owari, Chocoball, and..."

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.050
Was hiring her really the right decision?
